# DooRare compose environment
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and adjust. Docker Compose interpolates these into docker-compose.yml.
#
# Two supported modes:
#
# 1) LOCAL (default - no .env needed): `docker compose up -d --build` -> http://localhost:8080
#    The backend uses the Postgres `db` service (db / doorare / doorare_dev, no SSL) and NODE_ENV=development,
#    so BYOK falls back to the backend's built-in dev key. First run on an empty DB: `npm run db:reset` for mock data.
#
# 2) AWS / shared deploy (RDS): create `.env` with ALL of these - nothing points at RDS by default.
#    Provide the real values through the host environment or a secret store
#    (AWS Secrets Manager / SSM / ECS task secrets) - never commit them here.
#    NODE_ENV=production
#    DB_HOST=<rds-endpoint>
#    DB_PORT=5432
#    DB_NAME=doorare
#    DB_USER=<db-user>
#    DB_PASSWORD=<db-password>
#    DB_SSL=true
#    BYOK_ENCRYPTION_KEY=<openssl rand -hex 32>   (required in production; everyone on the same DB must share it)
#
# Optional:
# CORS_ORIGIN=https://your-host
# NODE_ENV=production
# FORECAST_JOB_ENABLED=false
# FORECAST_JOB_INTERVAL_DAYS=3
# FORECASTS_STALE_AFTER_DAYS=30
#
# Amazon Location Service / Cognito are set in docker-compose.yml for the deployed stack and can be overridden here:
# AWS_LOCATION_REGION=ap-southeast-1
# AWS_LOCATION_API_KEY=
# COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=
# COGNITO_APP_CLIENT_ID=
# COGNITO_REGION=us-east-1
#
# BYOK Encryption Key for AI Agent credentials (AES-256-GCM 64-hex key):
# BYOK_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
